The Apex Court dealing with this aspect of the matter in State of Orissa Vs. Gauranga Sahu reported in 2003 Crl. L.J. 3077 (SC) held as under:
"It is argued on behalf of the accused that mere dispatch of the report is not enough;
and that the prosecution is further obliged to prove that the letter so dispatched had reached the addressee, i.e. the accused.
